**Construction 8.3 (one common decoder at an absorption point).** At
$s\in\mathcal E_{\rm abs}$ use the preceding construction except
replace the $q_+$ live label and positive scalar failure label by one
label. Let $K$ be the actual **weighted** rank-two live matrix
associated with $\sqrt{w_+}q_+$. Here $w_+>0$ because the selector
is interior. TA.38 gives $b_+\ker K=0$. Define

$$
A_K=K^\dagger K+B_+,\quad S_K=(\ker K)^\perp,
\quad J_K:\mathbb C^2\longrightarrow S_K\text{ isometric}.
\tag{TA.44}
$$

Then $A_K$ has rank two and support $S_K$. Let $A_K^{+1/2}$ denote
its inverse square root on that support, zero on its kernel. Supply
one encoder and live/failure components of one decoder:

$$
\begin{aligned}
C_{\rm abs}&=J_K^\dagger A_K^{1/2}E^\dagger,\\
R_L&=KA_K^{+1/2}J_K,&R_f&=b_+A_K^{+1/2}J_K.
\end{aligned}
\tag{TA.45}
$$

Its decoder sends $X$ to $ER_LXR_L^\dagger E^\dagger$ in live
and to $\operatorname{tr}(R_fXR_f^\dagger)w_\ell g(t)dt\,P_f$
in each original failure label. The kernel condition gives the exact
identities

$$
R_LC_{\rm abs}=KE^\dagger,\quad
R_fC_{\rm abs}=b_+E^\dagger,\quad
R_L^\dagger R_L+R_f^\dagger R_f=I_2.
\tag{TA.46}
$$

Thus this is one common CP, full TP decoder on the whole dimension-two
fibre. No input-dependent normalization is used. Its encoder effect
is $E(K^\dagger K+B_+)E^\dagger$. Both its live and its failure
maps equal the former two maps exactly, on the full complex algebra,
not just their effects or twelve test-state values. The live and
failure height differences being merged are both positive, so their
actual-record absolute difference is preserved. Report plus on this
label. The added $B_+$ has zero $01$ coordinate and does not change
contrast. Negative spectral failure remains separate. There are
$4+1+1=6$ actual outcomes.

This proves the sufficiency direction of the kernel condition in
Lemma 3.2, for the entire spectral failure mass. The same formulas
also work with any positive multiple of $B_+$ when required.

